## 3. We established the comparison objective

You confirmed this objective:

> **Maximise critical detection while keeping false flags at or below 20%.**

The denominators matter:

| Metric | Calculation |
|---|---|
| Critical detection rate | Critical episodes flagged ÷ all human-critical episodes |
| False-flag rate | Noncritical episodes flagged ÷ all human-noncritical episodes |

For example, **49 / 274 = 17.9% false flags** means that 17.9% of the noncritical episodes were incorrectly flagged. It does **not** mean that only 17.9% of the model’s flagged episodes were wrong.

**Rationale:** without a false-flag constraint, a model could catch every critical episode simply by flagging everything. The constraint forces a useful tradeoff.

